{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ConeAngleIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConeAngleIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.offset_is_load_bearing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.offset_is_load_bearing","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L159-L177","doc":"A concrete instance showing the `π`-offset is load-bearing: with a `π/2`\noffset the complementary sum is `π`, not `2·π`, so the identity is falsifiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_add_sum_exteriorDihedral_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_add_sum_exteriorDihedral_mul","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**`nsmul` unfolded to a product** for downstream numerical use:\n`Θ(v) + ∑ exterior dihedral = (n : ℝ) · π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_eq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L134-L137","doc":"**Cone angle solved for.** `Θ(v) = n·π − ∑ exterior dihedral.` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_add_sum_exteriorDihedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.coneAngle_add_sum_exteriorDihedral","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L121-L132","doc":"**Rivin Lemma 1.2 (complementary form).** The cone angle and the total\nexterior dihedral around an interior vertex are complementary in `n·π`.\n\nThis is the falsifiable identity: it fails if the `π`-offset in `flat_rel` is\nwrong or if the incidence count `n = corners.card` is wrong.\n\n`-- Ref: [rivin2003] Lemma 1.2` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sum_exteriorDihedral_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sum_exteriorDihedral_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L110-L119","doc":"**Rivin Lemma 1.2 (exterior-sum form).** The total exterior dihedral around\nan interior vertex equals `n·π` minus the cone angle, where `n` is the number of\nincident corners.\n\n`-- Ref: [rivin2003] Lemma 1.2` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.flat_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.flat_rel","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Flat relation: exterior dihedral = `π` − interior contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.cone_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.cone_eq","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L104-L104","doc":"Cone angle = sum of the corner angles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.coneAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.coneAngle","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Total cone angle `Θ(v)` around the vertex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.exteriorDihedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.exteriorDihedral","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Exterior dihedral angle at each incident edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.interiorAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.interiorAngle","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Corner (interior) angle at the vertex contributed by each incident triangle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.corners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.corners","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Incident triangles / edges of the vertex star. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexStar","kind":"structure","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L84-L106","doc":"**The star of an interior vertex** of a Euclidean cone triangulation.\n\n`corners` indexes the incident triangles (equivalently, the incident edges, in\ncyclic bijection). `interiorAngle i` is the corner angle of triangle `i` at the\nvertex; `exteriorDihedral i` is the exterior dihedral at the corresponding edge;\n`coneAngle` is the total angle `Θ(v)` around the vertex.\n\nThe two geometric facts are carried as fields:\n* `cone_eq`  — the cone angle is the sum of the corner angles;\n* `flat_rel` — the exterior dihedral is `π` minus the interior contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sum_pi_sub_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sum_pi_sub_eq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConeAngleIdentity.lean#L69-L82","doc":"**Pure `Finset` skeleton.** Over any additive commutative group, if\n`g i = c - f i` on a finite index set `s`, then `∑ g = s.card • c - ∑ f`.\n\nThis is the offset-and-count bookkeeping with no geometry: `c` plays the role of\n`π`, `f` the interior angles, `g` the exterior dihedrals. It is non-trivial — it\nfails if the offset `c` is replaced inconsistently — and is the engine behind the\ngeometric identity below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}